  "worked_solution": "Notice that the given expression is a sum of squares, since\n\n$$\n16{p}^{12}+{m}^{10}={(4{p}^{6})}^{2}+{({m}^{5})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{p}^{12}+{m}^{10} & =16{p}^{12}-(-{m}^{10}) \\\\  & =16{p}^{12}-({i}^{2}{m}^{10}) \\\\  & ={(4{p}^{6})}^{2}-{(i{m}^{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =(4{p}^{6}+i{m}^{5})(4{p}^{6}-i{m}^{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
